Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:48:52 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(security): PR #5 review findings 1-6 (proposed
 correction, separate from PR #5)

1. approvalsV21 returns every matching V2.1 category; the first-match version
   re-created the approval short-circuit (rm --recursive && git -c alias push).
2. Computed command names: quoted $(...) in command position and variables
   assigned from a substitution used as the command name are hard-denied.
3. Path tokenizer keeps quoted words and escaped spaces (protected paths with spaces).
4. All per-user credential stores (.ssh, .npmrc, .aws, .azure, .kube, .gnupg,
   .docker, gh, id_*) denied; provider protects the credential directories.
5. Audit tool_use input: redact before truncating (no secret fragment at the cut).
6. Credential rule ignores quoted message data (git commit -m, echo, printf).
Tests: +24 (tests/unit/pr5-review-fixes.test.ts); unit 501/501.
